  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project 3.1: Integrated Solutions for preventing displacement and strengthening rural resilience (Nagaasho/CARE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen resilience in Somalia&apos;s rural communities affected by climate-related issues and to prevent internal displacement. The project is implemented by a consortium led by CARE Denmark. 

It aims to reach rural communities by promoting climate adaptation, livelihoods, and conflict prevention. Key interventions include: Climate-smart farming and water conservation training for farmers; Access to solar technologies, drought-resistant seeds, and green tools for women and youth; Local planning support using data and inclusive, environmentally conscious approaches; Entrepreneurship support via WFP&#x2019;s IFFS programme, with coaching and seed capital; Support for women-led cooperatives and value chains through microfinance.</narrative>
  </description>
